<title>ESTONIA: OMNITRAX STILL EYEING LOCAL RAILWAY - REPORT.</title>
<headline>OMNITRAX STILL EYEING LOCAL RAILWAY - REPORT.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. based rail operator Omnitrax remains interested in the privatisation of the railway freight operations in Estonia, Apripaev newspaper said on Friday.</p>
<p>Two representatives of Omnitrax, Patrick Broe of The Broe company which owns Omnitrax and Omnitrax managing director Dennis Lindburg comfirmed their company's interest, the daily said.</p>
<p>If privatisation goes ahead Omnitrax would seek the participation of local companies and named Pakterminal, a port handling company, as an exampale.</p>
<p>Arpipaev quoted Lindburg as saying that Omnitrax will conduct a technical study of the railway in autumn.</p>
<p>--Tallinn newsroom +372 620 9202 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
